{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013172-ascendant-exarchs-of-the-modern-age-the-chancellor-vs-the-eye","id":1013172,"title":"Ascendant Exarchs of the modern age: The Chancellor vs. The Eye","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-06T08:15:43-08:00","id":1013172,"title":"Ascendant Exarchs of the modern age: The Chancellor vs. The Eye","content":"Hello everyone, first post in the Mage subforum (and first in the OP forums for a while! Guess 2e really drew me back).<br /> <br /> I was reading (and loving) 2e and re-reading SotT when it struck me. Why is it that The Eye has been an Archgenitor for such a long time, and The Chancellor is only now rising?<br /> <br /> More to the point, does anyone else think finance, money and poverty have chained more souls and for a longer time than surveillance and eroding privacy?<br /> <br /> Given the above, I vacillate between reframing the Hegemony vs. Mammon conflict as Hegemony vs. Panopticon, or (barring explicit in-setting reasons against it) setting up an &quot;anti-Pentacle&quot; of five Greater Ministries.<br /> <br /> What does everyone else think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1714-the-butcher","name":"The Butcher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T08:35:09-08:00","id":1013185,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't buy that the Eye <i>has</i> been an Archigenitor that long. Surveillance as a major tool of mass control just isn't that old; busybodies poking their noses into their neighbours' business and policing social behaviour <i>is</i> old, but I don't think it's enough to give the Eye the symbolic weight to be an Archigenitor. My personal canon is that the Eye is the newest current Archigenitor, and replaced the Raptor, which was one of the oldest and reigned until being dethroned by modern medicine and mechanised agriculture. The Seers <i>claim</i> that the Eye was one of the Big Four all along, of course, but they <i>always</i> do that. The Architegnitors are eternal. We have always been at war with Eurasia.<br /> <br /> For an explanation of why the Chancellor is only now in a position to claim Archigenitor status, I would say that so long as finance and corporations were subject to and primarily tools of the state, too much of the Chancellor's domain was subject to the Unity for it to claim equal status. It's globalisation and the increasing ability of corporations to operate outside the control of any state, and to bend states to their will, that makes it possible for the Chancellor to demand a seat at the table... and naturally, the seat in question currently belongs to the Exarch whose thumb it has escaped from under.<br /> <br /> For that reason, incidentally, I feel that the Hegemony/Mammon conflict has a lot more symbolic weight than a hypothetical Hegemony/Panopticon one. I can't really see a basis for pitting the Form of nationalism and state power against the Form of mass surveillance; they go together like bread and butter, there's no conflict there at all. Nationalism and state power vs the unfettered power of money, though? Now you're talking.<br /> <br /> Edit: I don't see any problem with the idea of an anti-Pentacle of five Great Ministries, mind you, if that's the direction you want to go. AFAIK, there's no reason given why there have to be four and only four Iron Seals, that's just the way it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T11:32:36-08:00","id":1013291,"title":"","content":"Panopticon has only been a Greater Ministry since the 1950s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T11:54:03-08:00","id":1013299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013172-ascendant-exarchs-of-the-modern-age-the-chancellor-vs-the-eye?p=1013185#post1013185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK, there's no reason given why there have to be four and only four Iron Seals, that's just the way it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it has to do with Illuminati, secret masters of the world, with pyramid symbolism (the standard image of Egyptian pyramids have 4 sides after all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-06-2016, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T14:07:12-08:00","id":1013368,"title":"","content":"The other part to the story is that the Ministries are mortal institutions not simply reflections of society. Hegemony did a huge amount of damage to itself by attempting to bring in the Free Council. They're plausibly still the main ministry that the FC goes after.<br /> <br /> Further, the Seers aren't exactly the greatest people at HR. It's quite plausible the organisation has simply lasted beyond it's time. Too many old masters who don't know what they're doing and are too removed to care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T14:14:18-08:00","id":1013373,"title":"","content":"Another part of that is that the Seers are the ones who write their own history, and they have a nasty habit of writing the Archgenitors as having always been Archgenitors. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T14:18:30-08:00","id":1013375,"title":"","content":"Makes me wonder if the Pentacle don't make fun of them for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T14:27:14-08:00","id":1013382,"title":"","content":"As Above, So Below.<br /> <br /> As explained in Imperial Mysteries, if something exists in the Supernal, it always existed and will always exist, at least until it doesn't.<br /> <br /> If the Eye is an Archigenitor, he/she/it is always was an Archgenitor and always will be an Archgenitor, at least until a different Exarch claims the title. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T14:30:57-08:00","id":1013384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013172-ascendant-exarchs-of-the-modern-age-the-chancellor-vs-the-eye?p=1013375#post1013375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes me wonder if the Pentacle don't make fun of them for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to Archgenitors, it is not conducive to a long and happy life to poke it in the Eye. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T14:57:36-08:00","id":1013401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013172-ascendant-exarchs-of-the-modern-age-the-chancellor-vs-the-eye?p=1013373#post1013373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another part of that is that the Seers are the ones who write their own history, and they have a nasty habit of writing the Archgenitors as having always been Archgenitors. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Orders write their own history as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T15:44:05-08:00","id":1013445,"title":"","content":"Whaaaaaaat? Noooooo, the Pentacle would never re-write their own history in favore of a more potent Supernal narrative. Never. Never ever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T16:09:01-08:00","id":1013455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013172-ascendant-exarchs-of-the-modern-age-the-chancellor-vs-the-eye?p=1013291#post1013291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Panopticon has only been a Greater Ministry since the 1950s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I <i>have</i> to ask: who was the ministry that held primacy before Panopticon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T16:28:44-08:00","id":1013470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013172-ascendant-exarchs-of-the-modern-age-the-chancellor-vs-the-eye?p=1013455#post1013455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I <i>have</i> to ask: who was the ministry that held primacy before Panopticon?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not clear that there was one. Mage Noir seems to imply that Panopticon and Pantechnicon (I can't remember if that's the spelling) were fighting over becoming the fourth.<br /> <br /> It's possible that the idea of the four great ministries matching the four archigenitors is itself a recent invention. I mean, the idea of a ministry has only been around for about a quarter of the time the Seers have been around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T16:45:43-08:00","id":1013479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013172-ascendant-exarchs-of-the-modern-age-the-chancellor-vs-the-eye?p=1013445#post1013445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whaaaaaaat? Noooooo, the Pentacle would never re-write their own history in favore of a more potent Supernal narrative. Never. Never ever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, in this setting it is often difficult to draw a line between the Supernal and the Phenomenal World changing because of purposeful, planned manipulation by Supernal beings or mages, and as a spontaneous reflection of the actions Archmages, the Awakened, or mankind take. The Orders have a definite origin at a certain point in recorded history, yet their actions created a series of Supernal symbols tied to human archetypes to empower them that have always existed and always will exist, with various Ascended and a whole faction of Archmages to embody and protect them from the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> The only claim that remains questionable (and likely false by an omniscient perspective) is the claimed/supposed origin of the Orders in the Awakened organizations of the Time Before. But since the cosmic erasure of the Time Before, this has become an unkowable issue. Even if some Archmage were able to recreate some new version of Atlantis by Imperium, it would in all likelihood include some version of the Orders *now*, because the (living) symbols that empower them are too prominent and entrenched in the Supernal *now*.<br /> <br /> So in all likelihood at least half of the time the Pentacle and the Seers re-write their own history not to manipulate others and deceive themselves, but to reflect how the universe changes and evolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-06-2016, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T17:02:02-08:00","id":1013487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013172-ascendant-exarchs-of-the-modern-age-the-chancellor-vs-the-eye?p=1013479#post1013479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only claim that remains questionable (and likely false by an omniscient perspective) is the claimed/supposed origin of the Orders in the Awakened organizations of the Time Before. But since the cosmic erasure of the Time Before, this has become an unkowable issue. Even if some Archmage were able to recreate some new version of Atlantis by Imperium, it would in all likelihood include some version of the Orders *now*, because the (living) symbols that empower them are too prominent and entrenched in the Supernal *now*.<br /> <br /> So in all likelihood at least half of the time the Pentacle and the Seers re-write their own history not to manipulate others and deceive themselves, but to reflect how the universe changes and evolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>'The Silver Ladder is the Path to Victory' seems like more of an advertising slogan than a reflection of how the universe has changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}